{"id": "SGU_Episode_556", "title": "SGU Episode 556", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 556 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 556", "date": "March 5 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 3, "day": 5, "rogues": ["Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella", "George Hrab"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosalind_Franklin", "quote": "\n Science and everyday life cannot and should not be separated. \n", "quotee": "\n Rosalind Franklin \n", "quotee_title": "", "guests": [{"guest": "George Hrab", "guest_title": "", "guest_url": null}], "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-556", "episode_number": 556}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "", "title": "Flight Simulator", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:00:38", "hour": 0, "minute": "0", "second": "38", "title": "Flight Simulator"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 2, "text": "NECSS is also discussed", "title": "George's Upcoming Show", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:08:58", "hour": 0, "minute": "8", "second": "58", "title": "George's Upcoming Show"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 3, "text": "Norman Borlaug: Norman Borlaug was a plant geneticist who began the Green Revolution and is credited with saving a billion lives", "title": "Forgotten Superheroes of Science", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:14:44", "hour": 0, "minute": "14", "second": "44", "title": "Forgotten Superheroes of Science"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 4, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 5, "text": "https://www.sciencebasedmedicine.org/bad-reporting-about-uploading-memories/", "title": "Uploading Memories", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:22:24", "hour": 0, "minute": "22", "second": "24", "links": ["https://www.sciencebasedmedicine.org/bad-reporting-about-uploading-memories/"], "title": "Uploading Memories"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 6, "text": "http://www.latimes.com/science/sciencenow/la-sci-sn-scott-mark-kelly-nasa-twin-study-astronaut-20160301-story.html", "title": "A Year in Space", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:35:06", "hour": 0, "minute": "35", "second": "06", "links": ["http://www.latimes.com/science/sciencenow/la-sci-sn-scott-mark-kelly-nasa-twin-study-astronaut-20160301-story.html"], "title": "A Year in Space"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 7, "text": "http://www.ibtimes.co.uk/frbs-mystery-repeating-radio-signals-discovered-emanating-unknown-cosmic-source-1547133", "title": "Fast Radio Bursts", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:43:24", "hour": 0, "minute": "43", "second": "24", "links": ["http://www.ibtimes.co.uk/frbs-mystery-repeating-radio-signals-discovered-emanating-unknown-cosmic-source-1547133"], "title": "Fast Radio Bursts"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 8, "text": "http://medicalxpress.com/news/2016-03-pet-scans-reveal-key-alzheimer.html", "title": "Imaging Alzheimer\u2019s Disease", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:50:06", "hour": 0, "minute": "50", "second": "06", "links": ["http://medicalxpress.com/news/2016-03-pet-scans-reveal-key-alzheimer.html"], "title": "Imaging Alzheimer\u2019s Disease"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 9, "text": "http://www.dailygalaxy.com/my_weblog/2016/02/the-milky-ways-striking-symmetry-habitable-planets-more-than-5-billion-years-old-closer-to-galaxys-c.html", "title": "Galaxy Symmetry", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:55:19", "hour": 0, "minute": "55", "second": "19", "links": ["http://www.dailygalaxy.com/my_weblog/2016/02/the-milky-ways-striking-symmetry-habitable-planets-more-than-5-billion-years-old-closer-to-galaxys-c.html"], "title": "Galaxy Symmetry"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 10, "text": "Answer to last week: David Avocado Wolfe", "title": "Who's That Noisy", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:01:55", "hour": "1", "minute": "01", "second": "55", "title": "Who's That Noisy"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 11, "text": "Item #1: A 2015 review of lifecycle assessments of electric vehicles shows that overall they reduce green house gas emissions compared to gasoline vehicles.\nItem #2: A recent analysis finds that adoption of LED lights has led to a backfire effect in which total energy expenditure increases due to increased use of lighting.\nItem #3: A 2010 USDA report concludes that corn ethanol produces 2.3 BTUs of energy for every 1 BTU of energy used in production.\n", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:04:54", "hour": "1", "minute": "04", "second": "54", "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 12, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:27:06", "hour": "1", "minute": "27", "second": "06", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": [{"id": 13, "text": "Evan, take us home with a quote.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 14, "text": "Here we go:", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 15, "text": "\"Science and everyday life cannot and should not be separated.\"", "metadata": {"speaker": "<unknown>"}}, {"id": 16, "text": "Hear, hear!", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "GH", "speaker": "George Hrab"}}, {"id": 17, "text": "In just, more than a handful of words, really put a nice, succinct point on to it. Rosalind Franklin! Yes, one of our \u2013 yeah!", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 18, "text": "Yeah, baby! DNA! DNA!", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 19, "text": "Rosalind Avocado ...", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "GH", "speaker": "George Hrab"}}, {"id": 20, "text": "Right, not so forgotten Superhero of Science here on the Skeptic's Guide. English chemist, X-ray", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 21, "text": "Yay!", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "GH", "speaker": "George Hrab"}}, {"id": 22, "text": "crystallographer, made contributions to the understanding of the molecular structures of DNA, RNA, viruses, coal, and graphite.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 23, "text": "And totally got ripped off!", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 24, "text": "Yeah, got ripped off, yep. But,", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 25, "text": "Yeah", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 26, "text": "But, when you are asked, \u201cWho's a female scientist that you know?\u201d You don't have to just say Marie Curie.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 27, "text": "You can say Rosalind Franklin.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 28, "text": "Franklin.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 29, "text": "Yes.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 30, "text": "Awesome. All right, thanks Evan. George, always a pleasure to have you on the show, man.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 31, "text": "Thanks for having me on, guys. It's always fun.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "GH", "speaker": "George Hrab"}}, {"id": 32, "text": "See you soon, George!", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 33, "text": "Usually it is.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 34, "text": "Yeah.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "GH", "speaker": "George Hrab"}}, {"id": 35, "text": "Yeah, well, we'll see you at NECSS \u2013 I hope we're gonna see you before NECSS. We have", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 36, "text": "Hope so.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "GH", "speaker": "George Hrab"}}, {"id": 37, "text": "gotta work on the Extravaganza, to make it even more awesome.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 38, "text": "Oh yeah, we should probably talk about that, right?", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "GH", "speaker": "George Hrab"}}, {"id": 39, "text": "Oh, it's not an improv thing? Ooh, okay.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 40, "text": "We'll wing it.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 41, "text": "It's gonna be great.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "GH", "speaker": "George Hrab"}}, {"id": 42, "text": "Thank you all for joining me this week.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 43, "text": "Thank you, Doctor.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 44, "text": "Sure, Steve!", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 45, "text": "Thank you.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "GH", "speaker": "George Hrab"}}, {"id": 46, "text": "And until next week, this is your Skeptic's Guide to the Universe.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 47, "text": "The Skeptics' Guide to the Universe is produced by SGU Productions, dedicated to promoting science and critical thinking. For more information on this and other episodes, please visit our website at theskepticsguide.org, where you will find the show notes as well as links to our blogs, videos, online forum, and other content. You can send us feedback or questions to info@theskepticsguide.org. Also, please consider supporting the SGU by visiting the store page on our website, where you will find merchandise, premium content, and subscription information. Our listeners are what make SGU possible.", "metadata": {"links": ["http://www.theskepticsguide.org", "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/shop"], "speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}]}, {"id": 48, "text": "", "title": "References", "metadata": {"title": "References"}, "sections": []}]}